<title>CHILE: Chile posts slim trade deficit in May.</title>
<headline>Chile posts slim trade deficit in May.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chile reported a trade deficit of $56.3 million in May, compared to a surplus of $97.1 million in the same month of 1996, the Central Bank reported.</p>
<p>The new figure was a result of imports of $1.37 billion and exports of $1.32 billion during May, versus $1.39 billion and $1.48 last year respectively, the bank reported.</p>
<p>Cumulative figures and details were due to be released later by the bank.</p>
<p>(--Roger Atwood, Santiago newsroom +56-2-699-5595 x211))</p>
